cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these run records, please cite the paper."
title: "Structure, Not Just Magnitude, Drives the Damage from Misprojected LiDAR Depth Supervision in 3D Gaussian Splatting"
abstract: >-
  Analytic scenes with closed-form per-return co-visibility, used to separate the
  magnitude of cross-sensor depth-label error from its structure. Includes the 300-run
  analytic matrix, a 90-run nuScenes corroboration, a 90-run depth-sliced opacity probe
  of the damage mechanism with its per-view opacity maps, the 270 run records of the
  first pipeline version, and the scripts that apply the three frozen pre-analysis
  plans. The plan documents and the source-review audit records are not included.
